WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.360
Welcome to Grade 6 English, Unit 7: Nature’s Power.

2
00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:04.740
In this unit,

3
00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:11.640
you will explore the incredible and sometimes dangerous
forces of the natural world.You will learn about natural

4
00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:13.480
disasters such as cyclones,

5
00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:15.320
earthquakes, floods, droughts,

6
00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:22.220
and volcanic eruptions.You will discover how communities in
East Africa and around the world prepare for these events,

7
00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:27.160
respond when they strike, and
rebuild afterwards.Along the way,

8
00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:32.540
you will build a strong set of vocabulary
words related to planning, science, government,

9
00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:37.860
and community action.You will also
study an important grammar topic —

10
00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:45.720
how to use the Past Simple and Past Continuous tenses together,
joined by connecting words like while, when, and until —

11
00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:49.480
to describe events that happened at the same time in the past.

12
00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:55.400
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

13
00:00:56.240 --> 00:01:04.840
By the end of this unit, you will be able to use and understand
key vocabulary about natural forces, science, planning,

14
00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:06.640
government, and community.

15
00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:13.540
You will also read and discuss a text about natural
disasters and how communities respond to them.

16
00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:22.800
You will also identify the Past Simple tense (for completed
actions) and the Past Continuous tense (for actions that

17
00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:24.440
were happening when something else occurred).

18
00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:27.140
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

19
00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:35.060
Your vocabulary work begins with these words: creator,
dependency, descriptive, development, fuel, density.

20
00:01:35.980 --> 00:01:40.640
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

21
00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:44.180
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

22
00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:51.490
The reading sequence includes When Nature
Speaks and The Speech Under the Baobab, part 1.

23
00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:52.860
Read actively.

24
00:01:53.660 --> 00:01:58.520
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

25
00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:02.440
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

26
00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:07.840
The first language focus is Past Simple vs Past Continuous.

27
00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:12.260
The Past Simple describes actions that are finished.

28
00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:19.100
The Past Continuous describes actions that were happening
— still in progress — at a certain moment in the past.

29
00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:21.000
When we use them together,

30
00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:26.200
we can tell vivid stories about events that
happened at the same time or interrupted each other.

31
00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:31.020
This is especially useful when
describing natural disasters, emergencies,

32
00:02:31.540 --> 00:02:34.260
or any event where many things were happening at once.

33
00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:42.000
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

34
00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:47.553
In speaking, you will complete
Speaking 1: News Presenter Role-Play.

35
00:02:47.987 --> 00:02:52.920
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

36
00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:56.500
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

37
00:02:57.460 --> 00:03:00.480
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

38
00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:02.120
You are ready to begin.

39
00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:09.240
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

40
00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:11.940
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

41
00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:19.660
Use the AI tutor for hints and feedback any time, and
bring your questions to a live session too if you join one.
